/-!
# Analytification of differential forms and logarithmic forms

Let `X` be a smooth complex variety of dimension `n`, `X^an` its analytification and `E` a
reduced simple normal crossing divisor on `X`.

1. Every closed point `x` has an affine open neighbourhood `W` with regular functions
   `z₁, …, zₙ` forming a regular system of parameters at `x`, with `E ∩ W = {z₁ ⋯ z_k = 0}` and
   `dz₁, …, dzₙ` a basis of `Ω¹_W`; near every point `y` of `W^an` the functions `zᵢ - zᵢ(y)`
   are holomorphic coordinates of `X^an`.
2. With these charts `X^an` is a complex manifold, and `𝒪_{X^an}` is its sheaf of holomorphic
   functions.
3. In such a chart `(Ω^p_X)^an` is the sheaf of holomorphic `p`-forms, through an isomorphism
   carrying the image `s ⊗ 1` of an algebraic form `s` to `s^an`, and the holomorphic exterior
   derivative of `s^an` is `(ds)^an`.
4. On `W`, the logarithmic forms `Ω^p_X(log E)` are freely generated by the products of the
   `dzᵢ/zᵢ` (`i ≤ k`) and `dz_j` (`j > k`); their analytifications are the same products of
   holomorphic forms, which freely generate the holomorphic logarithmic forms, a module stable
   under the exterior derivative; and multiplying by the equation `z₁ ⋯ z_k` of `E` makes
   these forms holomorphic across `E`. The same holds for `Ω^p_X(log E)(-E)`: on `W` it is free
   on the forms `ω_I = (∏_{j ∉ I, j ≤ k} z_j) dz_I`, which are `z₁ ⋯ z_k` times the products
   above, and its analytification is carried isomorphically onto the holomorphic module freely
   generated by the `z₁ ⋯ z_k` multiples of the holomorphic products; and the analytification of
   the quotient `Ω^p_X / Ω^p_X(log E)(-E)` is carried isomorphically onto the quotient of the
   holomorphic `p`-forms by that module.

## Main results

* `MMP.Analytic.analytification_smooth_differentials`: the four statements above, as
  `IsAlgebraicComplexManifold` (2) and `HasAnalyticLogCoordinatesAt` at every closed point
  ((1), (3), (4)), about the manifold structure `analytificationChartedSpace`, the
  identification `structureSheafIsoHolomorphic` and the forms map `holomorphicFormsMap`.
* `MMP.Analytic.analytification_smooth_differentials_of_smoothOfRelativeDimension`: the same
  conclusions for a separated quasi-compact `ℂ`-scheme smooth of relative dimension `n`, not
  necessarily integral or connected.

## Implementation notes

* A complex manifold structure on `X^an` is a `ChartedSpace (EuclideanSpace ℂ (Fin n))`
  structure on its points with `IsManifold 𝓘(ℂ, EuclideanSpace ℂ (Fin n)) ∞`, Hausdorff and
  second countable; its sheaf of holomorphic functions is `𝒪[n, M]`. The identification
  `𝒪_{X^an} ≅ 𝒪[n, M]` is pinned by sending the analytification of a regular function `g` to
  the function `y ↦ g(y)`; the ringed-space identification of a chart with an open subset of
  `ℂⁿ` in (1) is this identification read through the chart.
* A holomorphic `p`-form on the chart `φ` over an open `O ⊆ ℂⁿ` is a family of continuous
  alternating maps `(ℂⁿ)ᵖ → ℂ` at the points of `φ⁻¹(O)` that, read through `φ`, extends to a
  complex-differentiable map on `φ(φ⁻¹ O)`; its exterior derivative is `extDeriv`. The
  isomorphism of (3) is an additive bijection of sections over every `φ⁻¹(O)`, compatible with
  restriction and linear over `𝒪_{X^an} ≅ 𝒪[n, M]`; it is pinned by its value on degree-zero
  algebraic forms and by its compatibility with the de Rham differentials, which determine it
  since the `dz_I` are iterated differentials of products of coordinates.
* Algebraic forms on an affine open `V` are read in `⋀^p Ω[Γ(X, V)⁄ℂ]` through
  `MMP.DeRham.formsAlgEquiv`. The logarithmic forms on `W` are `MMP.DeRham.logForms` of the
  ring `Γ(X, W)` inside the forms of `Γ(X, W ∖ E) = Γ(X, D(z₁ ⋯ z_k))`, and the products of
  the `dzᵢ/zᵢ` and `dz_j` are `ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti_family` of the logarithmic basis, indexed
  by the `p`-element subsets of `Fin n`. The holomorphic products are the alternatizations of
  the products of the coordinate functionals scaled by `1/zᵢ`.
* On the sections over `φ⁻¹(O)`, the analytification of `Ω^p_X(log E)(-E)` is the
  `𝒪_{X^an}`-span of the analytifications of the `ω_I` inside `(Ω^p_X)^an`: since the `ω_I` are
  free and the holomorphic module they generate is free, this is the module of sections of the
  analytified subsheaf. The quotient `Ω^p_X / Ω^p_X(log E)(-E)` is read on these sections as the
  quotient module of `(Ω^p_X)^an` by that span, and the holomorphic quotient by its holomorphic
  combinations; the comparison is stated as the bijectivity of the map induced by `Ψ`.

## References

* [Serre, *Géométrie algébrique et géométrie analytique*], §2.
* [Deligne, *Équations différentielles à points singuliers réguliers*], II.3.
-/

